G["Did you know about our \"Charitable Charms\" program?\n\nOfficial Crown event mascots like myself are authorized to distribute Lovely Charm Collector's Kits.\n\nYou can then use the Lovely Charms you gather to create Lovely Charm Bracelets for friends and loved ones, or turn them in to Lovely Merchants for Love Tokens!\n\nOne popular activity is making bracelets for your favorite leaders to let them know they're appreciated and adored..."]="Did you know about our \"Charitable Charms\" program?\n\nOfficial Crown event mascots like myself are authorized to distribute Lovely Charm Collector's Kits.\n\nYou can then use the Lovely Charms you gather to create Lovely Charm Bracelets for friends and loved ones, or turn them in to Lovely Merchants for Love Tokens!\n\nOne popular activity is making bracelets for your favorite leaders to let them know they're appreciated and adored..."
G["Did you know that Lin found the Hidden Master? He's in Paoquan Hollow."]="Did you know that Lin found the Hidden Master? He's in Paoquan Hollow."
G["Did you know that alchemists can transmute certain gems?  Mar'nah and I have been talking about this.\n\nI'm convinced that given her prowess, once her lab is complete, she and I will be able to create gems that were thought to be lost in time."]="Did you know that alchemists can transmute certain gems?  Mar'nah and I have been talking about this.\n\nI'm convinced that given her prowess, once her lab is complete, she and I will be able to create gems that were thought to be lost in time."
G["Did you know that the Barrens was once a lush forest? Thousands of years ago, before the first Sundering, it was verdant and thriving, watched over by the Kaldorei. But when the continents were torn apart, and this land became separated as what we call Kalimdor, this valley of nature became a harsh, sun-scorched plain.\n\nWhen I first learned this, I saw it as a great tragedy. I decided I would find a way to regrow the forests once more."]="Did you know that the Barrens was once a lush forest? Thousands of years ago, before the first Sundering, it was verdant and thriving, watched over by the Kaldorei. But when the continents were torn apart, and this land became separated as what we call Kalimdor, this valley of nature became a harsh, sun-scorched plain.\n\nWhen I first learned this, I saw it as a great tragedy. I decided I would find a way to regrow the forests once more."
