G["I wish I could make you a deal, partner - I really do - but you'll need to be exalted with the Bilgewater Cartel, first."]="Eu gostaria de poder fazer um acordo, parceiro - eu mesmo faço -, mas primeiro você precisará ser exaltado com o Cartel de Bilgewater."
G["I wish I could make you a deal, partner - I really do - but you'll need to be friendly with the Bilgewater Cartel, first."]="I wish I could make you a deal, partner - I really do - but you'll need to be friendly with the Bilgewater Cartel, first."
G["I wish I could pay today... but business has been so bad lately. I just don't have the money.\n\nThe few pieces of gold I have were going to buy dinner for my family. Please... there must be something you can do."]="I wish I could pay today... but business has been so bad lately. I just don't have the money.\n\nThe few pieces of gold I have were going to buy dinner for my family. Please... there must be something you can do."
G["I wish I could play ring toss."]="Tomara pudesse jogar ao lançamento de anilhos."
G["I wish I could tell you more, but until recently nobody believed such creatures existed. Long before the Titans shaped Azeroth into the world we see today, before the natural cycle of life and death as we know it, the Old Ones ruled over the elements and corrupted creation to serve their own malignant ends.\n\nFrom what Onu here tells me, the Titans ultimately defeated the Old Ones. Or, at least, they imprisoned them under the earth. Can something like that ever really die? I wish I knew more, but this is all pre-prehistory for me, and I've been around a while.\n\nI know that there are some that worship the Old Ones, if you can believe that. That's like praying for the end of the world. These Old Gods make people crazy!"]="I wish I could tell you more, but until recently nobody believed such creatures existed. Long before the Titans shaped Azeroth into the world we see today, before the natural cycle of life and death as we know it, the Old Ones ruled over the elements and corrupted creation to serve their own malignant ends.\n\nFrom what Onu here tells me, the Titans ultimately defeated the Old Ones. Or, at least, they imprisoned them under the earth. Can something like that ever really die? I wish I knew more, but this is all pre-prehistory for me, and I've been around a while.\n\nI know that there are some that worship the Old Ones, if you can believe that. That's like praying for the end of the world. These Old Gods make people crazy!"
G["I wish I could watch her reduce your pitiful band to cinders, but I am needed elsewhere. Farewell!"]="I wish I could watch her reduce your pitiful band to cinders, but I am needed elsewhere. Farewell!"
G["I wish I had a $gfather:mother; like you!"]="Tomara que tivesse um $gpadre: mãe; como você!"
