G["Mortal fools!  The ghouls of Deatholme will feast on your remains!"]="Mortal fools!  The ghouls of Deatholme will feast on your remains!"
G["Mortal heroes - your victory here today was foretold long ago. My brother's anguished cry of defeat will echo across the universe - bringing renewed hope to all those who still stand against the Burning Crusade."]="Mortal heroes - your victory here today was foretold long ago. My brother's anguished cry of defeat will echo across the universe - bringing renewed hope to all those who still stand against the Burning Crusade."
G["Mortal minds... So easily manipulated."]="Mentes mortais... Tão fáceis de manipular."
G["Mortal! You overreach."]="Mortal! You overreach."
G["Mortal, I want you to bear witness to this, but for your own safety stay back. Calen, you too."]="Mortal, quero que presencies isto, mas afaste-se pelo seu própria segurança. Calen, você também."
G["Mortal, take the dragon queen. Carry her to safety. Now! RUN! Get her away from here!"]="Mortal, take the dragon queen. Carry her to safety. Now! RUN! Get her away from here!"
G["Mortal? Yes I was once mortal. Weak.\n\nYou see my bonds now? These restraints are nothing compared to being shackled within a mortal coil.\n\nEven now the master's gifts stir within me, ready to be unleashed.\n\nNo, $c, my mortal days have passed, and if any flame of my former life still flickers within I would wish it extinguished. You'll have to do better than that, $r."]="Mortal? Yes I was once mortal. Weak.\n\nYou see my bonds now? These restraints are nothing compared to being shackled within a mortal coil.\n\nEven now the master's gifts stir within me, ready to be unleashed.\n\nNo, $c, my mortal days have passed, and if any flame of my former life still flickers within I would wish it extinguished. You'll have to do better than that, $r."
G["Mortals are..."]="Os mortais são..."
G["Mortals have no place here!"]="Aqui não há cabida para os mortais!"
G["Mortals that fancy themselves HEROES have entered the Broken Hall. Oh, I do hope this \"raid\" will amuse me more than the last."]="Uns mortais que se acreditam HERÓIS têm entrou na Câmera Partida. Oh, de verdade espero que esta \"Raide\" ao menos me divierta mais que a última."
G["Mortals! I cannot follow you any further - accept my blessing and use the Hourglass of Time to defeat Murozond!"]="Mortals! I cannot follow you any further - accept my blessing and use the Hourglass of Time to defeat Murozond!"
G["Mortals! You dare breach our inner sanctum. (Unbelievers. Heretics! Burn burn)\n You cross a threshold from which there is no return. (burn burn the heretics will burn.)"]="Mortals! You dare breach our inner sanctum. (Unbelievers. Heretics! Burn burn)\n You cross a threshold from which there is no return. (burn burn the heretics will burn.)"
G["Mortals, I am indebted to you for freeing me from the terrible corruption that besets this place. Though I have not yet recovered fully, I can help you battle Yogg-Saron.\nI can grant you and your friends the Fortitude of Frost, increasing your damage and reducing damage taken from enemy attacks. Should one of you be about to fall in battle, I can freeze you in a block of ice, protecting you from all damage for a short time. Know that this ability taxes my power, and I must rest after using it."]="Mortals, I am indebted to you for freeing me from the terrible corruption that besets this place. Though I have not yet recovered fully, I can help you battle Yogg-Saron.\nI can grant you and your friends the Fortitude of Frost, increasing your damage and reducing damage taken from enemy attacks. Should one of you be about to fall in battle, I can freeze you in a block of ice, protecting you from all damage for a short time. Know that this ability taxes my power, and I must rest after using it."
G["Mortals, I am indebted to you for freeing me from the terrible corruption that besets this place. Though I have not yet recovered fully, I can help you battle Yogg-Saron.\nI can grant you and your friends the Fury of the Storm, increasing your damage and maximum health. Should you be faced with evil so malevolent that it cannot be destroyed, I can channel all my power into a final Titanic Storm that will destroy even Immortals."]="Mortals, I am indebted to you for freeing me from the terrible corruption that besets this place. Though I have not yet recovered fully, I can help you battle Yogg-Saron.\nI can grant you and your friends the Fury of the Storm, increasing your damage and maximum health. Should you be faced with evil so malevolent that it cannot be destroyed, I can channel all my power into a final Titanic Storm that will destroy even Immortals."
G["Mortals, I am indebted to you for freeing me from the terrible corruption that besets this place. Though I have not yet recovered fully, I can help you battle Yogg-Saron.\nI can grant you and your friends the Resilience of Nature, increasing your damage and increasing healing taken from spells and effects. In addition, I can conjure Sanity Wells that will allow you to recover your Sanity when your grip on reality falters."]="Mortals, I am indebted to you for freeing me from the terrible corruption that besets this place. Though I have not yet recovered fully, I can help you battle Yogg-Saron.\nI can grant you and your friends the Resilience of Nature, increasing your damage and increasing healing taken from spells and effects. In addition, I can conjure Sanity Wells that will allow you to recover your Sanity when your grip on reality falters."
G["Mortals, I am indebted to you for freeing me from the terrible corruption that besets this place. Though I have not yet recovered fully, I can help you battle Yogg-Saron.\nI can grant you and your friends the Speed of Invention, increasing your damage and movement speed. In addition, I can destabilize the matrices of certain Saronite based life-forms, reducing their attack and casting speeds."]="Mortals, I am indebted to you for freeing me from the terrible corruption that besets this place. Though I have not yet recovered fully, I can help you battle Yogg-Saron.\nI can grant you and your friends the Speed of Invention, increasing your damage and movement speed. In addition, I can destabilize the matrices of certain Saronite based life-forms, reducing their attack and casting speeds."
G["Mortals, here?  What is the meaning of this, pathetic Broken!"]="Mortais, aqui? Que indica isto, patético Tábido!"
G["Mortals, you have saved me from a fate worse than death. Left to their devices, the sorcerers of the Lich King would have broken my will eventually, and condemned me to a tortured eternity of unlife. Ahead of you lies one who was not so fortunate: the once-proud consort of Malygos, Sindragosa.\n\nMortally wounded after Neltharion's betrayal and left to die alone in the snows of Icecrown, she exists now as a being of pure hatred. And yet, beneath those layers of malevolence still remains the noble spirit of a dragon queen. I believe there is yet hope that Sindragosa's soul may find peaceful respite."]="Mortals, you have saved me from a fate worse than death. Left to their devices, the sorcerers of the Lich King would have broken my will eventually, and condemned me to a tortured eternity of unlife. Ahead of you lies one who was not so fortunate: the once-proud consort of Malygos, Sindragosa.\n\nMortally wounded after Neltharion's betrayal and left to die alone in the snows of Icecrown, she exists now as a being of pure hatred. And yet, beneath those layers of malevolence still remains the noble spirit of a dragon queen. I believe there is yet hope that Sindragosa's soul may find peaceful respite."
G["Mortals, you merely separate the wheat from the chaff. (Unworthy, unworthy)."]="Mortals, you merely separate the wheat from the chaff. (Unworthy, unworthy)."
G["Mortals... They never cease to amaze me."]="Mortals... They never cease to amaze me."
G["Mortar strike called in. Let 'em have it, Hackel!"]="Mortar strike called in. Let 'em have it, Hackel!"
G["Mortar team, reload!"]="Mortar team, reload!"
G["Morthis! Thank Elune! I was worried I'd never see you again."]="Morthis! Obrigado a Eluna! Creí que nunca volvería a ver você."
G["Mortimer Moloch collapses from a heart attack!"]="Mortimer Moloch collapses from a heart attack!"
G["Most bad fortune with big hozen ravage. Makes for bad travels."]="Most bad fortune with big hozen ravage. Makes for bad travels."
G["Most bad fortune."]="Que mal sorte!"
G["Most definitely."]="Definitivamente que si."
G["Most definitely.  Might you mentor me?"]="claro. Será meu mentor?"
G["Most dragons would fear to tread here, $r.\n\nWhat could possibly bring a mortal to such a treacherous place?"]="Most dragons would fear to tread here, $r.\n\nWhat could possibly bring a mortal to such a treacherous place?"
G["Most esteemed Warchief -"]="Estimado Chefe de Guerra..."
G["Most good fortune to you, $r! My brother and I come from far away to share our luckydos."]="Most good fortune to you, $r! My brother and I come from far away to share our luckydos."
G["Most grummles keep a few luckydos about.\n\nLook, lint in pocket. Big luckydo. Oh, and smelly incense. Very big luckydo.\n\nNever trust unsmellible luck. Sometimes that is luck for someone else."]="Most grummles keep a few luckydos about.\n\nLook, lint in pocket. Big luckydo. Oh, and smelly incense. Very big luckydo.\n\nNever trust unsmellible luck. Sometimes that is luck for someone else."
G["Most impressive.  You are worthy to gain the rank of champion."]="Impressionante. Merece subir de grau e se juntar ao resto de Campeões."
G["Most of my brethren are disdainful of the Horde's \"barbaric\" ways, and I once counted myself among them. When I was first ordered to this somewhat humid and... fragrant place, I cursed my lot in life.\n\nDuring my studies, however, I grew to appreciate my surroundings. It has a certain charm, don't you think?\n\n...you wouldn't be interested in my studies, of course, not being a mage yourself."]="Most of my brethren are disdainful of the Horde's \"barbaric\" ways, and I once counted myself among them. When I was first ordered to this somewhat humid and... fragrant place, I cursed my lot in life.\n\nDuring my studies, however, I grew to appreciate my surroundings. It has a certain charm, don't you think?\n\n...you wouldn't be interested in my studies, of course, not being a mage yourself."
G["Most of my brethren are disdainful of the Horde's \"barbaric\" ways, and I once counted myself among them. When I was first ordered to this somewhat humid and... fragrant place, I cursed my lot in life.\n\nDuring my studies, however, I grew to appreciate my surroundings. It has a certain charm, don't you think?\n\nAh, and my studies, of course, were to allow other mages to return here with a spell. Shall I teach you?"]="Most of my brethren are disdainful of the Horde's \"barbaric\" ways, and I once counted myself among them. When I was first ordered to this somewhat humid and... fragrant place, I cursed my lot in life.\n\nDuring my studies, however, I grew to appreciate my surroundings. It has a certain charm, don't you think?\n\nAh, and my studies, of course, were to allow other mages to return here with a spell. Shall I teach you?"
G["Most of my debt was repaid... I think..."]="Most of my debt was repaid... I think..."
G["Most of my men were killed while infiltrating the Neferset borders.\n\nIt is my duty to make that sacrifice count for something."]="Most of my men were killed while infiltrating the Neferset borders.\n\nIt is my duty to make that sacrifice count for something."
G["Most of our steam tanks are out of commission and we're losing mountaineers quickly."]="A maioria de nossos tanques de vapor estão fosse de serviço e estamos perdendo montaraces rapidamente."
G["Most of the Alliance forces have left for Azeroth.  Hopefully the carefully-compiled reports that we sent with General Turalyon will make it back to Dalaran safely.\nNer'zhul's reckless portals have torn Farahlon apart, its green hills now quickly crumbling as the Twisting Nether corrupts the earth.  I have to find a passage back to the place I was before!"]="Most of the Alliance forces have left for Azeroth.  Hopefully the carefully-compiled reports that we sent with General Turalyon will make it back to Dalaran safely.\nNer'zhul's reckless portals have torn Farahlon apart, its green hills now quickly crumbling as the Twisting Nether corrupts the earth.  I have to find a passage back to the place I was before!"
G["Most of this stuff is beads and hides. Where's all the treasure?"]="Isto não são mais berloques e peles. Onde está o tesouro?"
G["Most people around these parts frown on lockpicking. As a little professional courtesy, let me show you a few tricks I've learned."]="Most people around these parts frown on lockpicking. As a little professional courtesy, let me show you a few tricks I've learned."
G["Most people hate swamps, but I know that they hold great secrets just beneath the murky surface."]="Most people hate swamps, but I know that they hold great secrets just beneath the murky surface."
G["Most rogues prefer to cloak themselves in the shadows, but not Helix."]="Most rogues prefer to cloak themselves in the shadows, but not Helix."
G["Motega, can I get another Water Explorer?"]="Motega, pode me dar outro explorador de água?"
G["Moth"]="Polilha"
