G["Technically speaking, that's not true, doctor. The rocks that fly out of a volcano like Mount Kajaro are called ejecta. It's not the sky. It's molten rock, or tephra. It cools as it descends, becoming lava bombs. Very appropriate, wouldn't you say?"]="Technically speaking, that's not true, doctor. The rocks that fly out of a volcano like Mount Kajaro are called ejecta. It's not the sky. It's molten rock, or tephra. It cools as it descends, becoming lava bombs. Very appropriate, wouldn't you say?"
