G["Would that we could all live like our most sacred emperor. That we could put aside all our burdens and exist in harmony with the cosmos. THAT, I believe, was his message to us... before he became one with the land, and hid Pandaria away from the terror of the Sundering."]="Quem dera pudéssemos todos viver como nosso tão santo imperador. Que pudéssemos nos livrar de todos os fardos e existir em harmonia com o cosmos. ESSA, eu creio, foi a mensagem dele para nós... antes de ele se unir à terra, e esconder Pandária do terror da Cisão."
G["Would you accompany me?"]="Would you accompany me?"
G["Would you believe I was laughed at when I began researching magic that would mask one's scent? It was deemed as impractical and a waste of time by the Arch-magi.\n\nWell, who is standing upwind of a devilsaur and laughing now? Ha!"]="Would you believe I was laughed at when I began researching magic that would mask one's scent? It was deemed as impractical and a waste of time by the Arch-magi.\n\nWell, who is standing upwind of a devilsaur and laughing now? Ha!"
G["Would you believe that in my darkest hour, at the apex of my being, I failed.\n\nAs I fled from the wanton destruction of the forces that overwhelmed us, the only sounds I could hear were the screams of my soldiers and the rapid beat of my own heart.\n\nA short while later, I returned to the Blasted Lands in hopes of rescuing my men and restoring my honor. Instead I was captured and beaten until dead.\n\nWhat I found out during my inquisition and subsequent torture was horrifying."]="Would you believe that in my darkest hour, at the apex of my being, I failed.\n\nAs I fled from the wanton destruction of the forces that overwhelmed us, the only sounds I could hear were the screams of my soldiers and the rapid beat of my own heart.\n\nA short while later, I returned to the Blasted Lands in hopes of rescuing my men and restoring my honor. Instead I was captured and beaten until dead.\n\nWhat I found out during my inquisition and subsequent torture was horrifying."
