G["You there, fetch water quickly! Get these flames out before they spread to the rest of the keep! Hurry, damn you!"]="You there, fetch water quickly! Get these flames out before they spread to the rest of the keep! Hurry, damn you!"
G["You there, have you filled your quota of lumber and elf ears today?!"]="You there, have you filled your quota of lumber and elf ears today?!"
G["You there, stop slacking!"]="You there, stop slacking!"
G["You there. You're welcome to take the contents of my cauldron. It was to be the second stage of my plan - amorous clothing."]="Eh! Pode pegar o que há dentro de meu caldeirão. Era a segunda parte de meu plano: roupa sensual."
G["You there... it is in your best interest to aid the Forsaken during these dire times.  Listen closely, as I dislike repeating myself.\n\nWe currently find ourselves in a dire shortage of cloth.  Bandages and simple textiles are running low, and donations are being accepted to bolster sagging inventories.  While you'll not receive financial compensation - hence what donation means - your aid will not go unnoticed."]="You there... it is in your best interest to aid the Forsaken during these dire times.  Listen closely, as I dislike repeating myself.\n\nWe currently find ourselves in a dire shortage of cloth.  Bandages and simple textiles are running low, and donations are being accepted to bolster sagging inventories.  While you'll not receive financial compensation - hence what donation means - your aid will not go unnoticed."
G["You think I do not know what you are trying to do? You think I haven't been watching you?"]="Acha que não sei o que intentas fazer? Acha que não te tenho estado observando?"
G["You think I know where Dalaran is, $Gbuddy:lady;? I can't even find my own tail! Sometimes it's there, sometimes it isn't.\n\nYou know what I heard though, $n?\n\nDook's got real since last time.\n\nI heard you went to Darnassus and got the Divine Bell.\n\nBut some human lady... Jana or somethin'... she got real mad!\n\nShe says the Horde betrayed her trust or something'... and she's kickin' all your people out of her city!\n\nOrc general Nazgrim say we need to help them vacuum... vacuate... err... evocate... err... get the ook out!"]="You think I know where Dalaran is, $Gbuddy:lady;? I can't even find my own tail! Sometimes it's there, sometimes it isn't.\n\nYou know what I heard though, $n?\n\nDook's got real since last time.\n\nI heard you went to Darnassus and got the Divine Bell.\n\nBut some human lady... Jana or somethin'... she got real mad!\n\nShe says the Horde betrayed her trust or something'... and she's kickin' all your people out of her city!\n\nOrc general Nazgrim say we need to help them vacuum... vacuate... err... evocate... err... get the ook out!"
G["You think I should have gone with the buzzsaw instead?"]="You think I should have gone with the buzzsaw instead?"
G["You think I'm being cruel to this worm?\n\nThey've killed two of my men this month!  We're too kind to this Wretched scum."]="You think I'm being cruel to this worm?\n\nThey've killed two of my men this month!  We're too kind to this Wretched scum."
G["You think I'm scared of you? I faced Onyxia!"]="Você acha que eu tenho medo de você? Eu encarei Onyxia!"
G["You think I've gone too far? There is no such thing. The Black Harvest will enslave the most powerful demons, draw on their power, and destroy all who oppose us, in this world, and on Azeroth! Do YOU mean to stop me, little one?"]="Você acha que eu fui longe demais? Isso não existe! A Colheita Negra escravizará os demônios mais poderosos, drenará seus poderes e destruirá a todos que se oponham a nós neste mundo e em Azeroth! VOCÊ acha que pode me impedir, criaturinha?"
G["You think after doing such good work on Stormwind Harbor I'd get a bit of slack from this dwarf...\n\nI just want to get this statue up the ramp and back in place as fast as possible.  But she's got a complaint every step of the way.  Her solution to every problem is to blow it up.  It feels like I'm working with a gnome or a goblin.  But at least they'd be sober.\n\nLook at our work crew, no discipline.  You know why?  Because she undermines me!\n\nA bad attitude, a lazy crew... This isn't going to be a quick fix at all."]="You think after doing such good work on Stormwind Harbor I'd get a bit of slack from this dwarf...\n\nI just want to get this statue up the ramp and back in place as fast as possible.  But she's got a complaint every step of the way.  Her solution to every problem is to blow it up.  It feels like I'm working with a gnome or a goblin.  But at least they'd be sober.\n\nLook at our work crew, no discipline.  You know why?  Because she undermines me!\n\nA bad attitude, a lazy crew... This isn't going to be a quick fix at all."
G["You think it is so easy to vanquish your fears?"]="You think it is so easy to vanquish your fears?"
G["You think maybe one day, Kekek lead Frenzyheart home, like bear-men fight to get tree-city back? Kekek want own home, not city with purple men, not jungle with big-tongues."]="You think maybe one day, Kekek lead Frenzyheart home, like bear-men fight to get tree-city back? Kekek want own home, not city with purple men, not jungle with big-tongues."
G["You think me to be mad, do you? Yes... yes, perhaps a little.\n\nYou see, even after eight hundred and seventy-seven years of quietude, the desire to breathe does not go away.\n\nPerhaps something went wrong with my encasement. Perhaps it was my... preternaturally keen intellect. Whatever the cause, I was fully aware of the passage of time during my years in the amber.\n\nAfter seventy-eight years, I stopped trying to escape. I kept my mind sharp by creating and solving puzzles. The amber took care of the rest of my body.\n\nBut my sanity? No, I cannot say with good confidence that it survived intact."]="You think me to be mad, do you? Yes... yes, perhaps a little.\n\nYou see, even after eight hundred and seventy-seven years of quietude, the desire to breathe does not go away.\n\nPerhaps something went wrong with my encasement. Perhaps it was my... preternaturally keen intellect. Whatever the cause, I was fully aware of the passage of time during my years in the amber.\n\nAfter seventy-eight years, I stopped trying to escape. I kept my mind sharp by creating and solving puzzles. The amber took care of the rest of my body.\n\nBut my sanity? No, I cannot say with good confidence that it survived intact."
G["You think ookin' is nasty word? You ain't ikkin' know anything."]="You think ookin' is nasty word? You ain't ikkin' know anything."
G["You think that was bad? You shoulda been here, oh, thirty years ago, I'd say.\n\nOne o' the boys left his lunch out - some kind of fish stew, if mem'ry serves.\n\nWell he leaves it out in the atrium - BIG ol' pot o' fish stew, I'm sure of it now - and, cub's honor, every hozen within a hundred miles come a-runnin'.\n\nAfter cleanin' THAT up, I'll take some overgrown nibblers any day..."]="You think that was bad? You shoulda been here, oh, thirty years ago, I'd say.\n\nOne o' the boys left his lunch out - some kind of fish stew, if mem'ry serves.\n\nWell he leaves it out in the atrium - BIG ol' pot o' fish stew, I'm sure of it now - and, cub's honor, every hozen within a hundred miles come a-runnin'.\n\nAfter cleanin' THAT up, I'll take some overgrown nibblers any day..."
